 [case id=048-triple-quote-backslash-bijection level=extended
  [tags triple-quoted string escape bijection roundtrip canonical-2-4]
  [desc [#
Triple-quoted strings are VERBATIM (lexicon §5 [L31]): the source `\"` is the
two bytes backslash + quote, NOT an escaped quote. On canonical emit the
backslash must be re-escaped (`\\`) because the following `"` would otherwise
re-decode as an escape — the minimal re-escape (canonical.md §2.4) that keeps
parse(emit(x)) ≡ x. The `"` itself needs no escape inside `'...'`.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[x """a\"b"""]
#]]
  [out-ast [#
{"type":"Document","elements":[{"type":"Element","name":"x","items":[{"type":"Text","value":"a\\\"b"}]}]}
#]]
  [out-xml [#
<x>a\"b</x>
#]]
  [out-cx [#
[x 'a\\"b']
#]]
 ]

 [case id=049-canonical-backslash-fixed-point level=extended
  [tags string escape bijection idempotent canonical-2-4]
  [desc [#
The canonical form from case 048 is a FIXED POINT: emitting the re-parsed value
reproduces it byte-for-byte, so parse(emit(parse(s))) ≡ parse(s) holds across
any number of text stages in a pipeline (the R3 regression).
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[x 'a\\"b']
#]]
  [out-ast [#
{"type":"Document","elements":[{"type":"Element","name":"x","items":[{"type":"Text","value":"a\\\"b"}]}]}
#]]
  [out-xml [#
<x>a\"b</x>
#]]
  [out-cx [#
[x 'a\\"b']
#]]
 ]
]
